<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Affliction Warlock Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>DPS trinkets are very straightforward, as their performance is not affected by Warlock-specific buffs. As a result, direct-damage trinkets should generally be used on cooldown unless timed with specific boss mechanics that increase damage taken. Stat-increasing trinkets should similarly either be used on cooldown or aligned with burst phases (e.g., <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=113860/dark-soul-misery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Soul: Misery</span></a>).<br/>
<br/>As Phase 1 progresses, Celestial Dungeons will become available shortly after each raid tier is released. This makes the LFR versions of raid trinkets accessible to all players and provides upgrades over both of the active trinkets listed below.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>While the specific type of trinket (active vs. passive) isn't overly critical for Warlocks, passive trinkets are inherently easier to use and maintain uptime on, making them ideal for players who may forget to use actives or have inconsistent cooldown alignment.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> is your end goal for the second trinket slot. It offers a large amount of Intellect and a powerful Haste proc. However, it won't be available until <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6067/terrace-of-endless-spring">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Terrace of Endless Spring</span></a> opens.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is one of the strongest trinkets early in Phase 1. While it starts as best-in-slot, it will eventually be replaced by raid trinkets once <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6067/terrace-of-endless-spring">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Terrace of Endless Spring</span></a> opens. Its main drawback is the initial cost, though prices are expected to drop as the phase progresses.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87065/light-of-the-cosmos">
<img alt="Light of the Cosmos" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Light of the Cosmos</span></a> is your best option until <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> becomes available. It has a secondary stat (instead of Intellect) as its passive, with an Intellect proc. While slightly weaker due to its item level and stat profile, it's still a powerful pre-raid choice.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> offers valuable Hit Rating while you're still gearing, allowing you to prioritize offensive secondary stats elsewhere. It's also easily farmed from Heroic Dungeons, making it a strong early pickup.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a>, available from the Shado-Pan reputation vendor, performs similarly to <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> and can be used as an alternative if you have excess Valor. However, it has limited value once better trinkets become available.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Affliction Warlocks in Phase 1</span></h2>Reputation gear is strong, but prioritizing the proper factions is key.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Shado-Pan (Honored)</b>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89077/cloak-of-snow-blossoms">
<img alt="Cloak of Snow Blossoms" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cloak of Snow Blossoms</span></a>: The best pre-raid cloak available. This cloak will likely last well into early raid content, making Honored with Shado-Pan a high priority.</div></li></ul>
<b>The Klaxxi</b>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89062/klaxxi-lash-of-the-orator">
<img alt="Klaxxi Lash of the Orator" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Klaxxi Lash of the Orator</span></a> (Honored): A strong and accessible pre-raid belt.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98073/leggings-of-the-poisoned-soul">
<img alt="Leggings of the Poisoned Soul" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leggings of the Poisoned Soul</span></a> (Revered): Solid leggings for early gearing, though eventually replaced by <b>Tier 14 legs</b>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90859/seal-of-the-lucid">
<img alt="Seal of the Lucid" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_147.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of the Lucid</span></a> (Exalted): A great ring if you reach Exalted before securing a better alternative, and does not require Valor.</div></li></ul>
<b>Golden Lotus</b>
<ul class="exclude-units">
