<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Affliction Warlocks</span></h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>In Mists of Pandaria, spellcasters require <b>15% Spell Hit</b> to ensure their spells do not miss raid bosses. This means your direct spell abilities (like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=30108/unstable-affliction">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unstableaffliction_3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unstable Affliction</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48181/haunt">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warlock_haunt.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunt</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146739/corruption">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_abominationexplosion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corruption</span></a>, etc.) will always land once this cap is reached.<br/>
<br/>At level 90, this 15% Hit corresponds to approximately <b>5100 Hit Rating</b>. Note that this is slightly less for Humans and Gnomes if they use their respective racial weapons.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>For spellcasters in MoP, <b>Expertise also contributes to your Spell Hit chance</b>, up to the same 15% cap. This was a change introduced in Patch 5.0.4 to allow hybrid classes and specific gear setups to use Expertise as a viable stat for casters. Note that this also means that on items with Hit Rating, you can reforge another secondary stat to Expertise, increasing your total Hit Chance on items that already have the stat present.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Expertise and Hit Rating are interchangeable up to the 15% total Spell Hit cap</b>. After that, any excess in either stat provides no benefit.<br/>
<br/>This also means gear with Expertise can be valuable to a caster until you're capped, especially useful in early gearing or PvP gear sets.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Affliction Warlocks</span></h2>Warlocks will often ignore socket colors if the bonus isn't strong enough. In general, we prefer to use red <b>Intellect</b> gems, unless there's a compelling reason not to. However, <b>early on during gearing</b>, when your overall stats are lower, <b>Hit and Haste have a higher relative value than Intellect</b>. This makes <b>green and yellow gems</b> with Hit or Haste particularly valuable for reaching key rating caps.<br/>
<br/>A good rule of thumb: <b>if the socket bonus is less than 20 Intellect or 30 of any rating stat</b>, it's often better to ignore the bonus and socket the strongest gem instead. That said, <b>this depends on your current gear and stat balance</b>, you should simulate your character to determine the most optimal gemming strategy.<ul class="exclude-units">
